{"id": "EUVD-2026-102969", "enisaUuid": "00020f84-a792-3e07-bb5f-4896d335890a", "description": "Antiword through 0.37 contains a stack out-of-bounds read vulnerability in vGet8PapInfo and vGet8ChrInfo in prop8.c because FKP run counts and grpprl offsets are not bounded. Attackers can supply a crafted .doc file with malicious FKP pages to read past the 512-byte stack buffer, crashing antiword or corrupting style parsing.", "datePublished": "2026-10-16T17:39:37", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-18T12:26:11", "baseScore": 4.8, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:L/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:P/VC:N/VI:N/VA:L/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://hackmd.io/@haindpwn/antiword-word8-plcflst-count-and-fkp-run-oob-read", "https://github.com/rsdoiel/antiword/blob/fe4b579067122a2d9d62647efb1ee7cfe3ca92bb/prop8.c#L997-L1022", "https://github.com/rsdoiel/antiword/blob/fe4b579067122a2d9d62647efb1ee7cfe3ca92bb/prop8.c#L1461-L1474", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/antiword-through-0.37-stack-out-of-bounds-read-via-prop8-c-fkp-parsing"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-111678", "GHSA-gmg3-h7rv-2cc6"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "7793857a-a96a-3e23-b493-c46f83062f86", "product": {"name": "antiword", "vendor": {"name": "Adri van Os"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22640.37"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "4c01fa94-601a-3f7c-92aa-4007be215490", "vendor": {"name": "Adri van Os"}}], "isExploited": false}